md5 constant 
K[64]:
	i in 0 -> 63:
		K[i] = floor(2**32 * abs(sin(i + 1)))
s[ 0..15] := { 7, 12, 17, 22,  7, 12, 17, 22,  7, 12, 17, 22,  7, 12, 17, 22 }
s[16..31] := { 5,  9, 14, 20,  5,  9, 14, 20,  5,  9, 14, 20,  5,  9, 14, 20 }
s[32..47] := { 4, 11, 16, 23,  4, 11, 16, 23,  4, 11, 16, 23,  4, 11, 16, 23 }
s[48..63] := { 6, 10, 15, 21,  6, 10, 15, 21,  6, 10, 15, 21,  6, 10, 15, 21 }

digestion: prend un hex 512bit (128 hchar)
decoupe en fragments de 32bit (8 hchar) F[16]
static A=F[0]
static B=F[1]
static C=F[2]
static D=F[3]

64 iteration (i):
if i < 16:
    j = i
if i < 32:
    j = (5*i + 1) % 16
if i < 48:
	j = (3*i + 5) % 16
else:
	j = (7*i) % 16

B->C'
C->D'
D->A'
B' = redbox(F(B, C, D, i) + A + fragment of current iteration F[j], i, B) // combine


F fct (B C D i):
  if i < 16:
	return (B & C) | ((~B) & D)
  if i < 32:
    return (D & B) | ((~D) & C)
  if i < 48:
	return B ^ C ^ D
  return C ^ (B | (~D))

redBox fct (input, i, B):
	res = input + K[i]
	res = input << s[i]
	res = input + B

if end:
	result = A' . B' . C' . D'
else
	A = A'
	B = B'
	C = C'
	D = D'


Padding function:
	add '1' bit onto message, pad with '0' bit until blength is 448 % 512
	to fill remaining 64 bit:
		append original msg length in bits % 2**64 into message


usage:
pad message,
for each 512 bloc, run digestion BUT is 
	- ABCD static ?
	- ABCD equal to ABCD0 (first fourth fragment of first  512 block)
		at end of digestion add ABCD to ABCD0 (for each digestion or only from 2?)